full-query: "Your company owns an on-premises Ubuntu server in a local data center where several legacy applications are running. You want to use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy new application revisions to this particular on-premises instance but firstly you need to register the server in CodeDeploy and use an IAM user to perform the authentication. Which of the following methods is the most appropriate?"
